mintland (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remove dead-end river tributaries: the water network is now a single
    calm chain between lakes, with no branches ending in the middle of
    the sheet.
  * Keep lakes a little farther from the bottom edge than from the other
    edges, leaving room for the Cinnamon panel and its Start button.
  * Check the full castle sprite footprint before placing a town, so no
    road ends at an empty spot under an icon island.
  * Cap the icon clearance slider at 70 px.

 -- Alex <smartor777@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:27:44 +0300

mintland (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release "Old map" as a finished theme: dense hand-drawn parchment
    world with castle towns, forests, mountain ranges, rivers, lakes,
    sailing ships, a lighthouse, a witch's hut with cat and ravens.
  * Draw castles as a tight cluster of steep-roofed houses with a tall
    central tower and flag.
  * Build the water network from the placed lakes: one chain through all
    lakes, meandering arcs, thin tributaries that taper out, and no
    self- or mutual intersections.
  * Keep lakes fully inside the sheet and clear of the icons.
  * Give the icon islands a light parchment fill and a real pixel slider
    (4-120 px) for the clearance around icons.
  * Add sliders for bird count and keep roads a small distance clear of
    the icon islands.
  * Split baking into a static base and a cheap icon overlay, so moving
    an icon no longer redraws the whole scene.
  * Move xprop/gio/xwininfo polling into background threads so the GTK
    main loop and the WebKit frame clock never stall.
  * Cache-bust the theme scripts as well as the page.
  * Show the package version in the switcher window title.

 -- Alex <smartor777@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0300

mintland (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the "Old map" theme: a dense hand-drawn parchment world with
    castles, forests, mountains, rivers, lakes and moving carts.
  * Rebuild only the icon overlay when icons move; the static map stays
    baked, so dragging icons no longer redraws the whole scene.
  * Register worldmap in themes.json and the switcher with density,
    forest, castles/roads and carts controls.
  * Build the map around icon clearings: trees, roads and castles avoid
    icon rectangles instead of being covered by an opaque patch.
  * Rebuild the world shortly after an icon stops moving, not mid-drag.
  * Show the package version in the switcher window title.
  * Add sailing boats to every lake: small, upright, gently rocking.
  * Add a witch's hut with a circling raven in the emptiest part of the map.
  * Move lakes away from icon islands when icons are dragged, and pull the
    rivers to the new lake centres.
  * Keep forest trees off the roads, so dotted road lines stay readable.
  * Modernise the lake boat into a three-masted sailing ship.
  * Add a lighthouse with a slowly turning beam on the largest lake.
  * Add a pumpkin and a "Witch" label beside the witch's hut.
  * Redraw the compass rose with 16 points and N/S/E/W letters.
  * Pace animation frames evenly instead of skipping every other one.
  * Move xprop/gio/xwininfo polling into background threads so the GTK
    main loop and the WebKit frame clock never stall.
  * Lighten the icon islands, keep them free of trees, and add an
    "Icon island size" slider.
  * Add more parchment stains and faded patches to the paper.
  * Paint the stains as irregular noise blobs instead of even circles.
  * Keep the whole sprite footprint out of icon islands, not just the feet.
  * Fill icon islands as solid squircles so no gaps show between icons.
  * Darken the compass rose and draw it above the icon islands.
  * Scatter small parchment specks across the sheet instead of large
    dark patches.
  * Fill icon islands with the main map parchment colour.
  * Let water flow around icon islands instead of cutting off at them.
  * Make the icon island slider a real pixel offset (6-52 px).
  * Route rivers with A* over their waypoints: the path stays simple
    (no self-intersections) and keeps a clear margin from icon islands.
  * Keep every lake fully inside the sheet and clear of icon islands.
  * Widen the icon clearance slider to 4-120 px.
  * Add a birds slider for the ravens over the witch's hut.
  * Add a sitting cat beside the witch's hut.
  * Draw dark edges on roads so they read over dense forest.
  * Add short water channels between nearby lakes.
  * Keep the lake boat steady: no per-frame rotation.
  * Keep a wider margin between lakes and the sheet edge.
  * Cache-bust the theme scripts, not just the page.
  * Allow only one water channel per lake, and build channels after
    rivers so they never cross a river.
  * Count bridges over lake channels as well as rivers.
  * Draw fields with hatched furrows instead of empty diamonds.
  * Give bridges a deck, planks and railings.
  * Keep roads a small distance clear of the icon islands.
  * Redraw castles as a tight cluster of steep-roofed houses with a
    tall central tower and flag, like the reference map.
  * Add thin river tributaries that taper out and lead nowhere.
  * Build the water network from the placed lakes: one chain through
    all lakes, meandering arcs, no self- or mutual intersections.
  * Let birds fly over the whole map, not only above the witch's hut.

 -- Alex <smartor777@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:50:00 +0300

